**Backup restore gap found and closed, 2026-07-18.** User asked "is there anything remaining to build on the backend" — a full-repo audit (dedicated subagent, code-verified not memory-verified) found sub-project 7 had backup CREATION (`buildInstanceBackup` + `/admin/backup`) but no restore counterpart, despite the original implementation plan explicitly calling for a `pnpm restore-backup` CLI. Built it: `server/src/export/restore.ts` + `server/src/scripts/restore-backup.ts`. Deliberately a CLI, not an HTTP endpoint (restoring over a live instance is not a button) — hard-refuses on a non-empty instance, no override flag. Preserves original IDs (true restore, not import). E2e-verified with a genuine two-database live round-trip. All other candidate gaps (cloud backups, cli-visualizer #9, cross-file call-graph, symbol embeddings, Leiden) confirmed as deliberate, already-documented deferrals.

**Pre-production hardening pass, same day.** User asked "anything else to be concerned about" then "yes fix them" — didn't just document, actually built/verified: (1) booted the real ONNX embedding path (`NODE_ENV=production`) for the first time all session — it had silently never run, every test used the fake embedder; confirmed real semantic search works (conceptual match with zero shared keywords). (2) Wrote + built + ran a real Dockerfile against real docker-compose Postgres over real HTTP — colima needed 2GB→6GB, `onnxruntime-node`'s native install OOM's at 2GB. (3) `@fastify/helmet` + env-gated `@fastify/cors` (same-origin-only by default), tested. (4) `.github/dependabot.yml`. (5) Consolidated the single-process-architecture assumption (lockout/embedding-queue/extraction-queue/permission-kick-bus/MCP-rate-limit/repo-poller are all in-process state) into one doc section in `docs/agents/implementation.md` — documented as a known constraint, NOT built out to be distributed (that would be premature scaling work with no deployment need yet). Found a real bug mid-PR: `.gitignore`'s `.env.*` rule was silently excluding `.env.example` itself. 129 tests green, all on prod.

